      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-251408",
      ":question/problem": "Two teachers independently evaluated the school projects of six students, ranking the projects based on student performance. The table below shows the rankings, where the students are labeled $A$-$F$.\n\n|  | A | B | C | D | E | F |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| **Rank (Teacher 1)** | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| **Rank (Teacher 2)** | $1$ | $5$ | $6$ | $4$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n\nCalculate Spearman's correlation coefficient $r_{s}$ and interpret the result.\n\nRounded to two decimal places, $r_{s} \\approx$ {{field-1}}. Therefore, we conclude that there is\n{{field-2}} between the rankings.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
