      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-251416",
      ":question/problem": "The school projects of twenty students are evaluated independently by two teachers. Each teacher ranks the projects independently, assigning a unique integer between $1$ and $20$ to each project. If $d_{1}, d_{2}, \u2026, d_{20}$ are the differences between the ranks given to each student, and the sum of the squared differences is given by\n$\u2211_(i = 1)^(20)d_{i}^{2} = 780$\n\nthen find the Spearman's rank correlation coefficient $r_{s}$ and interpret the result.\n\nRounded to two decimal places, $r_{s} \\approx$ {{field-1}}. Therefore, we conclude that there is\n{{field-2}} between the rankings.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
    }
